WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.739
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.822 --> 00:32.115
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.199 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:34.034 --> 00:35.869
[beeping]

00:36.787 --> 00:37.788
[confirmation beep]

00:38.789 --> 00:40.749
FINAL EPISODE

00:45.754 --> 00:48.090
COLLABORATION ON LICENSING
THE BEAUTÉ DEPARTMENT STORE IN YONGDU

00:48.173 --> 00:49.675
SECURITY LEVEL: STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL

00:49.758 --> 00:51.260
[♪ gripping tense music playing]

00:51.343 --> 00:54.346
[Sungwoo's dad] You should
take the fall for this.

00:54.429 --> 00:56.139
You'll hear from a prosecutor.

00:57.474 --> 01:00.102
[door opens, closes]

01:00.185 --> 01:01.937
[Sungwoo] That damn mayor of Yongdu...

01:02.020 --> 01:04.231
He acted all high and mighty
about running for president.

01:05.148 --> 01:06.858
And now, look at the mess he caused.

01:06.942 --> 01:09.027
Looks like you'll be the one
putting up with this.

01:09.111 --> 01:10.112
I feel bad for you.

01:10.195 --> 01:12.197
Someone has to take responsibility.

01:14.074 --> 01:17.411
[scoffs] Since I am the CEO,
I should be the one taking responsibility.

01:17.494 --> 01:18.537
But as you know,

01:18.620 --> 01:20.664
all the paperwork and accounts
were created by you.

01:20.747 --> 01:22.374
So, I don't think
there's anything I can do.

01:22.457 --> 01:23.458
DELIVERED BY BAEK SANGHYEON

01:31.216 --> 01:33.927
[safe-deposit box door closes, beeps]

01:34.011 --> 01:35.846
[Sungwoo sighs, clicks tongue]

01:36.847 --> 01:37.848
Sanghyeon.

01:38.849 --> 01:40.976
If you get through this,

01:41.059 --> 01:42.936
my dad will make it worth your while.

01:44.271 --> 01:47.107
You know that
from everything he's done for you.

01:47.649 --> 01:49.985
Honestly, he's given you in folds
compared to what you've done.

01:50.068 --> 01:51.153
Don't you agree?

01:51.236 --> 01:52.487
Hey.

01:52.571 --> 01:56.116
You milked that gold ring prank
that I pulled when we were young.

02:00.078 --> 02:02.164
I've always been grateful to Chairman.

02:02.706 --> 02:03.749
And to you, too.

02:04.249 --> 02:05.250
Up until now,

02:07.002 --> 02:10.380
I didn't have to worry about money
or about going hungry.

02:11.006 --> 02:12.382
It's all thanks to you.

02:14.760 --> 02:16.887
I wasn't trying to get credit or anything.

02:20.182 --> 02:21.266
[sighs]

02:22.100 --> 02:23.143
Hey, Sanghyeon.

02:24.561 --> 02:26.271
You're smart,

02:26.355 --> 02:27.939
so you know what to say
to the prosecutors.

02:28.023 --> 02:29.691
[♪ gripping tense music playing]

02:32.944 --> 02:34.279
I trust you.

02:36.573 --> 02:37.699
Nice tie, man.

02:39.201 --> 02:40.369
Sungwoo.

02:48.919 --> 02:50.087
Did you ever,

02:50.921 --> 02:52.631
even once, think of me as your friend?

02:52.714 --> 02:53.757
What are you talking about?

02:57.719 --> 02:58.970
Of course, we're friends.

02:59.680 --> 03:00.889
You and I are the same age.

03:00.972 --> 03:02.641
Not like that.

03:03.058 --> 03:06.436
Not as a tool for you to use
every time you get yourself in trouble...

03:08.480 --> 03:10.649
but have you ever
thought of me as a real friend?

03:11.149 --> 03:13.360
Geez, what's with you today?

03:14.695 --> 03:17.698
Hey, we're friends, aren't we?

03:18.407 --> 03:19.533
[chuckles]

03:23.704 --> 03:25.372
[low whirring, gentle bubbling]

03:32.879 --> 03:34.131
[Sungwoo] Of course, we're friends.

03:34.214 --> 03:35.382
You and I are the same age.

03:35.465 --> 03:36.758
What did I expect?

03:49.980 --> 03:51.565
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

03:51.648 --> 03:52.983
[pellets rattle in bottle]

03:53.733 --> 03:57.154
If you received a favor,
just repay them exactly what you owe.

03:57.237 --> 03:58.697
I think anything beyond that is excessive.

03:58.780 --> 04:02.159
I guess I don't really know
how much you owe them,

04:02.242 --> 04:04.661
but haven't you worked hard enough
that it's all been paid off?

04:04.744 --> 04:06.246
Then you don't need
to do any more for them.

04:10.125 --> 04:11.293
[places bottle on table]

04:11.376 --> 04:12.461
[sighs]

04:13.420 --> 04:15.046
[reporter 1] Yes. I'm on the way now.

04:15.130 --> 04:16.214
[reporter 2] Get moving!

04:16.840 --> 04:18.049
[reporter 3] Yes, I'm here.

04:18.133 --> 04:19.134
[reporter 4] Get inside!

04:19.217 --> 04:20.802
[reporters clamoring]

04:20.886 --> 04:22.179
[reporter 5] Hurry up and come in!

04:22.262 --> 04:24.890
4TH-GENERATION HEIR OF MYUNGSOONDANG
KIM WOOJU'S FRAUD SCANDAL EXPOSED

04:24.973 --> 04:26.850
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

04:27.684 --> 04:29.728
I greet all you respectable journalists.

04:30.270 --> 04:33.732
I'm Kim Wooju,
an ordinary man who lives in Seoul.

04:38.904 --> 04:42.699
I stand here today to expose the successor
of a mid-sized company

04:43.283 --> 04:45.577
breaking up a family with his affairs
and attempt to make

04:46.495 --> 04:50.707
an illegal profit of millions.
I believe his immoral and unjust act

04:51.750 --> 04:52.959
must come out.

04:53.710 --> 04:56.421
4TH-GENERATION HEIR OF MYUNGSOONDANG
KIM WOOJU'S FRAUD SCANDAL EXPOSED

04:56.505 --> 04:59.132
I'm sure you all know this bakery.

04:59.216 --> 05:00.509
That's right.

05:00.592 --> 05:02.219
It's Myungsoondang.

05:03.678 --> 05:04.930
And this man...

05:05.013 --> 05:08.683
He is the head of their marketing team,
and the chairwoman's grandson.

05:08.767 --> 05:10.185
His name is Kim Wooju.

05:10.268 --> 05:11.311
KIM WOOJU

05:11.394 --> 05:12.729
And this woman

05:13.230 --> 05:15.148
is currently my legal wife,

05:15.524 --> 05:17.108
and her name is Yoo Meri.

05:17.609 --> 05:20.987
And this document is
the proof of our marriage.

05:21.613 --> 05:23.198
A few months ago,

05:23.281 --> 05:26.034
from the Beauté Department Store
raffle event held for newlyweds,

05:26.117 --> 05:28.829
she won a five-million-dollar house
at Beauté Palace...

05:30.372 --> 05:31.373
Wait a minute.

05:32.749 --> 05:34.835
[softly] The property value
must've gone up.

05:36.253 --> 05:37.254
[remote clicks]

05:39.464 --> 05:41.758
[inhales deeply, exhales]

05:42.509 --> 05:44.386
PROPERTY SALE PRICE GRAPH

05:44.845 --> 05:46.304
It's 5.7 million dollars now?

05:46.388 --> 05:48.056
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

05:48.640 --> 05:49.641
[clears throat]

05:50.851 --> 05:52.519
Rounding up to six million dollars.

05:52.602 --> 05:53.854
-Six million...
-[phone vibrating]

05:54.729 --> 05:57.065
MERI

05:57.148 --> 05:58.567
-[scoffs]
-[phone continues vibrating]

05:58.650 --> 05:59.943
You're too late, Meri.

06:00.986 --> 06:02.320
This will be the end of you.

06:05.824 --> 06:07.909
She won a six-million-dollar house

06:08.577 --> 06:09.828
at Beauté Palace.

06:10.579 --> 06:12.414
[automated voice] The call cannot
be connected. Transferring to...

06:12.497 --> 06:14.124
[clicks tongue] Oh, my gosh.
[sighs deeply]

06:14.207 --> 06:16.585
[automated voice] The call cannot
be connected. Transferring to...

06:16.668 --> 06:17.711
[line disconnects]

06:23.049 --> 06:24.259
What?

06:24.342 --> 06:25.594
A press conference?

06:25.677 --> 06:27.053
I got a call from him.

06:27.470 --> 06:29.514
I think he's going to cause trouble.

06:30.181 --> 06:31.308
Where is he?

06:31.391 --> 06:33.101
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

06:37.522 --> 06:38.940
[tires screeching]

06:50.118 --> 06:52.203
-[reporter 1] He's here.
-[reporter 2] He's coming.

06:52.787 --> 06:54.706
[reporter 3]
Was it lobbying on behalf of the company?

06:54.789 --> 06:57.167
[reporter 4] Is it true that you followed
orders from Beauté Group CEO?

06:57.250 --> 06:58.543
Did you create illegal lobbying funds

06:58.627 --> 07:00.045
-for the mayor of Yongdu?
-[reporter 3] Please, a word.

07:00.128 --> 07:01.546
What do you think of this incident?

07:01.630 --> 07:02.964
What's your relation to it?

07:03.048 --> 07:04.049
[inhales deeply]

07:04.132 --> 07:06.009
I cooperated fully with the investigation.

07:09.262 --> 07:10.722
-Wait.
-[reporter 5] One more thing...

07:10.805 --> 07:12.057
[reporters clamoring]

07:17.062 --> 07:18.146
Just one more comment.

07:18.229 --> 07:20.732
-Are you acknowledging it then?
-Please wait!

07:21.983 --> 07:23.276
Excuse me.

07:23.360 --> 07:24.736
[reporters clamoring]

07:39.959 --> 07:42.921
MISSED CALL
CEO

07:46.299 --> 07:47.801
CEO

07:49.469 --> 07:51.304
[bangs table] You bastard!

07:52.263 --> 07:53.807
What do you think you're doing?

07:54.974 --> 07:56.476
I acknowledged the part I played.

07:56.559 --> 07:59.104
Then why is the prosecution asking for me?

07:59.979 --> 08:01.856
Because I didn't admit
to things I had no hand in.

08:01.940 --> 08:03.400
What the heck are you saying?

08:03.817 --> 08:05.443
[♪ gripping tense music playing]

08:05.985 --> 08:06.986
Hey.

08:07.696 --> 08:08.697
You talked, didn't you?

08:09.656 --> 08:10.657
[sighs regretfully]

08:11.241 --> 08:13.660
This is why they say
you should never trust the ungrateful.

08:14.244 --> 08:16.913
How could you repay
our kindness like this, you trash?

08:16.996 --> 08:19.624
I think I repaid you enough
for what you've done for me.

08:19.833 --> 08:21.251
I'll pay for my own sins.

08:22.001 --> 08:23.878
So, you should pay for your own sins.

08:25.046 --> 08:26.673
-[line disconnects]
-Hey, Baek.

08:27.590 --> 08:28.633
Baek Sanghyeon!

08:31.720 --> 08:32.846
Goddamn it!

08:36.683 --> 08:38.518
EXPOSED

08:39.894 --> 08:41.104
[clears throat]

08:42.897 --> 08:44.774
I greet all you respectable journalists.

08:44.858 --> 08:46.860
I'm Kim Wooju...

08:47.986 --> 08:50.030
[clears throat]
an ordinary man who lives in Seoul.

08:51.573 --> 08:52.574
[sighs softly]

08:53.116 --> 08:55.201
I stand here today to expose the successor
of a mid-sized company

08:55.285 --> 08:57.328
for breaking up a family
with his affairs...

08:57.996 --> 08:59.080
[breath trembling]

08:59.164 --> 09:00.498
Wait a minute.

09:01.583 --> 09:02.667
This jerk...

09:02.751 --> 09:04.836
Did he expose everything
including the Beauté Palace?

09:04.919 --> 09:06.671
-[knock at door, door opens]
-[sighs anxiously]

09:08.965 --> 09:10.091
Hey!

09:10.175 --> 09:12.802
You know the Beauté Palace winner.

09:12.886 --> 09:14.429
You mean Ms. Yoo Meri?

09:14.512 --> 09:16.097
Yes, her. [breathing heavily]

09:16.473 --> 09:18.266
-Did we transfer the ownership?
-Not yet.

09:18.349 --> 09:20.226
Three months isn't up yet,
we need a few more days.

09:20.310 --> 09:21.561
-[yells] Hurry it up!
-Okay.

09:21.644 --> 09:24.314
If they find out
that it was a lobbying gift...

09:24.397 --> 09:25.398
Pardon?

09:26.024 --> 09:27.067
[panting]

09:27.734 --> 09:28.735
I mean...

09:29.527 --> 09:32.363
People might get the wrong idea.

09:33.281 --> 09:36.659
So, transfer the ownership
and make sure there's nothing suspicious.

09:36.743 --> 09:37.744
Okay, sir.

09:37.827 --> 09:38.995
That was for the raffle.

09:39.079 --> 09:40.538
It had always been for the raffle.

09:40.622 --> 09:41.956
-Got it?
-Yes, sir.

09:42.040 --> 09:43.917
-[yells] Have you got it?
-Yes, for the raffle.

09:46.294 --> 09:47.712
-Oh, sir?
-[panting softly]

09:48.671 --> 09:50.173
There's something more urgent.

09:52.092 --> 09:53.176
What now?

09:54.385 --> 09:56.513
-It's this...
-[sighs anxiously]

09:58.306 --> 09:59.891
PRESS RELEASE
FOR KIM WOOJU'S PRESS CONFERENCE

10:02.560 --> 10:05.230
Some crazy guy sent an email to the press,

10:05.313 --> 10:08.441
saying that he'll expose
how the raffle event was a fraud.

10:10.235 --> 10:11.361
A press conference?

10:12.445 --> 10:13.863
-[chuckles]
-[chuckles nervously]

10:18.284 --> 10:19.452
Go and prevent it now.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.412
If this hits the media,

10:21.496 --> 10:23.289
people will start
focusing on Beauté Palace.

10:23.873 --> 10:25.375
-Okay.
-If they dig up anything,

10:25.458 --> 10:27.127
it'll blow back on me in no time.

10:27.210 --> 10:28.795
-Do you get me?
-Yes, sir.

10:28.878 --> 10:29.921
If you get it, hurry up.

10:30.004 --> 10:31.047
Okay.

10:32.423 --> 10:33.591
[line ringing]

10:35.718 --> 10:37.595
-[line connects]
-Is this the head of the legal team?

10:38.304 --> 10:39.681
It's an emergency.

10:42.934 --> 10:44.018
[chuckles nervously]

10:45.562 --> 10:47.856
4TH-GEN HEIR OF MYUNGSOONDANG
KIM WOOJU'S FRAUD SCANDAL EXPOSED

10:48.690 --> 10:49.816
[sighs softly]

10:56.781 --> 10:58.116
Did they not get my email?

11:01.244 --> 11:02.328
[sighs deeply]

11:03.204 --> 11:04.789
YONGDU CITY, BEAUTÉ

11:08.793 --> 11:11.004
BEAUTÉ DEPARTMENT STORE SUSPECTED
OF GIVING ILLEGAL POLITICAL FUNDS

11:13.089 --> 11:14.090
Beauté?

11:14.174 --> 11:15.675
EX-MAYOR BYEON JONGSIK
INDICTED FOR BRIBERY

11:15.758 --> 11:17.177
AND VIOLATION OF THE POLITICAL FUNDS ACT

11:17.260 --> 11:18.761
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

11:25.810 --> 11:26.853
[door opens]

11:33.610 --> 11:34.903
-Get rid of it.
-Yes, sir.

11:34.986 --> 11:36.237
Take off the banner.

11:36.321 --> 11:38.406
And take photos as evidence.

11:38.489 --> 11:39.824
Wait a minute.

11:39.908 --> 11:40.909
Hey, wait...

11:43.119 --> 11:44.621
What are you doing?

11:44.704 --> 11:46.497
We're from the legal team
of Beauté Department Store.

11:47.749 --> 11:48.791
STATEMENT OF COMPLAINT

11:48.875 --> 11:52.045
We're suing you for defamation
and interference with business.

11:53.004 --> 11:54.005
What?

11:59.552 --> 12:01.638
You called in the press
to spread false information, right?

12:02.305 --> 12:03.890
To say that there was
a fake newlywed couple

12:03.973 --> 12:05.934
who received the prize
at our company's event.

12:06.017 --> 12:07.560
[Wooju] Oh, that...

12:07.644 --> 12:09.103
That's not false information.

12:09.187 --> 12:10.813
I have proof.

12:10.897 --> 12:12.398
Truth doesn't matter.

12:12.482 --> 12:14.817
If it's true,
it's defamation for revealing facts,

12:14.901 --> 12:17.028
and if it's false,
it's defamation for spreading lies.

12:17.737 --> 12:18.780
Either way,

12:18.863 --> 12:21.074
the moment our department store
is mentioned,

12:21.574 --> 12:24.035
we'll estimate the business loss
caused by defamation

12:24.118 --> 12:25.578
and file a claim for damages.

12:26.871 --> 12:27.872
"Claim for damages"?

12:31.709 --> 12:34.128
One, two, three, four...

12:34.754 --> 12:36.256
10 million dollars? [breath trembling]

12:37.590 --> 12:38.925
-Wait, please.
-Hey, stop.

12:39.008 --> 12:41.010
-Sir, you need to move.
-[Wooju] Please wait!

12:41.094 --> 12:42.095
[yelps]

12:42.971 --> 12:44.055
[thuds]

12:44.806 --> 12:46.099
It's all true.

12:46.182 --> 12:48.101
-Please hear me out!
-You'll get hurt.

12:48.184 --> 12:49.394
Please wait!

12:49.477 --> 12:50.645
[yelps]

12:50.728 --> 12:52.188
Wait, please!

12:52.855 --> 12:53.898
Oh, gosh.

12:54.691 --> 12:56.276
[man] I told you you'd get hurt.

12:57.151 --> 12:58.236
[Kim Wooju sighs]

13:01.906 --> 13:03.574
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

13:10.707 --> 13:11.708
[sniffles]

13:14.252 --> 13:15.795
[crying] I don't have this money.

13:15.878 --> 13:16.879
CLAIM: 10 MILLION DOLLARS

13:20.675 --> 13:21.718
[sighs]

13:34.480 --> 13:35.606
Wooju.

13:44.073 --> 13:45.074
Meri.

13:45.158 --> 13:46.159
[sighs softly]

13:46.993 --> 13:49.620
Did you tell the department store?
[breath trembling]

13:49.996 --> 13:52.123
What did you say
that caused all this fuss?

13:52.206 --> 13:54.125
I only found out by coming here.

13:56.419 --> 13:57.503
So, it wasn't you?

14:02.383 --> 14:03.384
Meri... [breath trembling]

14:03.926 --> 14:05.887
Can I ask you to think over this again?

14:06.471 --> 14:07.472
[chuckles nervously]

14:07.722 --> 14:09.682
I don't have any money.

14:09.766 --> 14:10.767
You...

14:10.850 --> 14:12.894
You know well that I can't sleep

14:12.977 --> 14:15.772
when I get things like this
because it makes me so anxious.

14:16.272 --> 14:17.690
Don't be like this.

14:17.774 --> 14:19.859
Could you please talk to Beauté

14:19.942 --> 14:21.736
and ask them to drop the lawsuit?

14:21.819 --> 14:23.863
How am I supposed to do that?

14:23.946 --> 14:25.531
There's nothing I can do, either.

14:26.240 --> 14:27.909
[sobbing] Please, Meri.

14:31.245 --> 14:32.705
For old times' sake.

14:33.623 --> 14:35.166
No... [sniffles]

14:35.708 --> 14:36.709
You and I...

14:38.044 --> 14:39.462
We were lovers once.

14:40.671 --> 14:41.672
Please?

14:41.756 --> 14:44.092
Why did you have to take things this far?

14:44.175 --> 14:46.344
What made you take it this far?

14:46.427 --> 14:47.762
[sobbing]

14:54.852 --> 14:56.562
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

14:58.856 --> 15:00.191
[continues sobbing]

15:05.446 --> 15:06.614
I know.

15:09.283 --> 15:10.952
I know because I was like that.

15:13.037 --> 15:14.789
You did this because you hate me.

15:20.419 --> 15:22.797
Still, you shouldn't have
done this to him.

15:24.966 --> 15:25.967
[sniffles]

15:29.095 --> 15:30.096
Wooju.

15:32.390 --> 15:33.391
These days,

15:34.225 --> 15:36.269
I'm really happy and at ease.

15:38.396 --> 15:40.731
I think I like him a lot.

15:42.150 --> 15:43.276
So...

15:44.068 --> 15:46.362
I want you to be happy, too.

15:48.406 --> 15:49.448
[sniffles]

15:51.325 --> 15:54.370
I wish you'd move on from all this.

15:54.912 --> 15:58.124
Seeing you broken
and falling apart like this

15:58.207 --> 15:59.625
doesn't make me happy

16:01.002 --> 16:02.128
or satisfied.

16:02.211 --> 16:03.296
[sobbing]

16:05.631 --> 16:07.425
[♪ heartfelt, melancholy music playing]

16:08.926 --> 16:11.220
Let's forget that you hurt me

16:12.346 --> 16:14.015
and your hatred toward me.

16:16.601 --> 16:18.519
Let's forget it all...

16:21.314 --> 16:23.399
and just keep the good memories.

16:24.567 --> 16:25.568
How about that?

16:26.611 --> 16:28.321
Can you do that for me?

16:38.497 --> 16:39.874
[sobbing]

16:43.336 --> 16:46.255
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

16:48.549 --> 16:49.800
[digital queue alert chimes]

16:52.220 --> 16:53.971
FAMILY REGISTRATION

16:54.055 --> 16:55.556
-Hello.
-[clerk] Hi.

16:56.015 --> 16:57.141
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

17:02.897 --> 17:04.732
DIVORCE DECREE

17:04.815 --> 17:06.234
[mouse clicking, keyboard clacking]

17:10.196 --> 17:11.572
It's been submitted.

17:11.656 --> 17:12.740
Thank you.

17:13.824 --> 17:15.284
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

17:26.420 --> 17:27.505
[sighs in relief]

17:35.805 --> 17:37.098
[sighs deeply]

17:45.690 --> 17:46.732
[car horn honks]

18:13.467 --> 18:14.552
Get in.

18:25.980 --> 18:27.023
[♪ upbeat pop music fades]

18:37.825 --> 18:40.369
This is it
since the house was already furnished.

18:40.828 --> 18:42.288
-[digital beep]
-Shall we get going then?

18:51.047 --> 18:52.131
[both sigh]

18:52.214 --> 18:54.008
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

18:54.091 --> 18:57.428
So much has happened at this place.

19:03.851 --> 19:04.852
Let's go.

19:26.248 --> 19:29.293
Hello, Ms. Yoo Meri.
I'm calling from Beauté Department Store.

19:30.169 --> 19:31.212
[Meri exclaims]

19:32.213 --> 19:34.507
Did you not hear from Mr. Baek?

19:35.883 --> 19:36.884
Pardon?

19:37.259 --> 19:38.260
A divorce?

19:38.844 --> 19:41.764
Yes, I got a divorce.

19:41.847 --> 19:43.974
Because I'm no longer a newlywed,

19:44.892 --> 19:46.977
I don't have the right to keep the prize.

19:47.061 --> 19:48.104
[Mr. Kwon] Wait, hold on.

19:48.187 --> 19:50.314
But we need to transfer the ownership.

19:50.398 --> 19:52.024
Can't we just give it to you?

19:52.108 --> 19:55.236
[hesitates] But I'm not fit for it,
so I can't accept it.

19:56.028 --> 19:57.113
I'm really sorry.

19:57.196 --> 19:59.949
-[stutters] No, that's not... Ms. Yoo...
-[line disconnects]

20:00.032 --> 20:01.325
Ms. Yoo... She...

20:02.326 --> 20:03.661
[stutters] She hung up.

20:05.788 --> 20:07.456
-Was that Beauté?
-Yes.

20:08.082 --> 20:10.126
I wonder if Mr. Baek didn't report it.

20:10.793 --> 20:12.253
Beauté seems to be unaware of it.

20:12.336 --> 20:15.047
They're chaotic right now
because of the illegal lobbying funds.

20:15.131 --> 20:17.133
[acknowledging] I saw it on the news.

20:18.259 --> 20:20.845
Anyway, aren't you sad?

20:21.721 --> 20:22.972
You mean about the house?

20:23.472 --> 20:25.599
[inhales deeply] I am.

20:26.517 --> 20:27.810
I really am.

20:28.936 --> 20:31.605
When will I ever get to live
in a house like that?

20:33.023 --> 20:34.024
But...

20:34.608 --> 20:39.363
I found something
much more precious than that.

20:39.447 --> 20:40.531
What's that?

20:42.783 --> 20:43.826
You know what it is.

20:43.909 --> 20:45.953
I really don't. What is it?

20:46.620 --> 20:47.913
Never mind if you don't.

20:47.997 --> 20:49.248
What is it?

20:50.249 --> 20:51.876
Let's just listen to some music.

20:51.959 --> 20:53.127
[both chuckle]

20:54.086 --> 20:55.504
-Okay.
-[digital beep]

20:55.588 --> 20:57.882
-Play something upbeat.
-[digital beep]

20:57.965 --> 20:59.633
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

20:59.717 --> 21:00.926
[chuckles]

21:05.306 --> 21:07.600
Wow, the sound system is great.

21:07.683 --> 21:08.851
It's amazing, right?

21:09.769 --> 21:11.562
-It's quite expensive.
-[both laugh]

21:19.528 --> 21:20.613
[clatters]

21:33.417 --> 21:35.795
MANAGING DIRECTOR BAEK SANGHYEON

21:43.677 --> 21:44.887
-[phone vibrating]
-[clangs]

21:47.973 --> 21:50.184
YOON JINGYEONG

21:51.811 --> 21:52.812
Yes, hello?

22:03.781 --> 22:04.782
[sighs]

22:07.785 --> 22:09.453
What happened?

22:09.537 --> 22:10.830
I saw the news.

22:13.457 --> 22:17.127
Regarding Mr. Kim Wooju,
it'll be swept under the rug.

22:18.128 --> 22:19.797
If it's revealed
that it was for the bribe,

22:20.464 --> 22:22.383
the company will also be in trouble.

22:23.342 --> 22:24.969
So, you don't need to worry about it.

22:25.052 --> 22:26.428
That's not it.

22:28.931 --> 22:30.975
I'm worried about you.

22:31.809 --> 22:33.727
According to the news,

22:33.811 --> 22:35.271
they said you came clean.

22:36.480 --> 22:38.649
You told me to pay for my sins
and live without shame.

22:39.149 --> 22:40.985
When did I say that?

22:41.610 --> 22:43.195
[chuckling softly] Maybe I heard it wrong.

22:43.279 --> 22:44.655
What I meant was,

22:44.738 --> 22:47.032
in the world of crime,

22:47.116 --> 22:48.993
it's only right
that virtue triumphs over vice

22:49.076 --> 22:50.494
and justice prevails.

22:51.620 --> 22:55.541
Well, I was only telling you to take
responsibility for what you did wrong,

22:55.624 --> 22:57.209
not for the things you didn't.

22:57.293 --> 22:58.335
[chuckles softly]

22:58.711 --> 23:00.087
That's what I did.

23:00.880 --> 23:03.507
I only acknowledged
the things that I did wrong.

23:03.591 --> 23:05.301
Just like you told me to.

23:06.302 --> 23:08.679
So, what happens now?

23:09.597 --> 23:11.515
[inhaling deeply] Well...

23:12.016 --> 23:13.851
Since I'm under
non-custodial investigation,

23:14.351 --> 23:15.936
I'm sure they'll reach a verdict soon.

23:16.812 --> 23:17.855
Don't tell me...

23:18.939 --> 23:21.650
You're not actually going
to prison or anything, right?

23:22.401 --> 23:24.320
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

23:24.987 --> 23:26.030
[sighs softly]

23:27.865 --> 23:29.241
[Sanghyeon sighs in despair]

23:29.325 --> 23:30.618
The night view looks

23:31.619 --> 23:33.579
especially beautiful tonight.

23:40.252 --> 23:41.253
I think...

23:43.631 --> 23:46.842
I'll think of you a lot from time to time.

23:51.180 --> 23:52.389
[sighs deeply]

23:55.684 --> 23:57.853
Can I ask you a favor?

24:08.781 --> 24:09.782
Can you call her?

24:10.240 --> 24:11.492
Yes, ma'am.

24:13.202 --> 24:15.162
[Songhee] I think it's better
with the shadows.

24:15.245 --> 24:16.497
-[Meri] Should we try?
-Twenty...

24:16.580 --> 24:18.040
-[phone ringing]
-Negative 30.

24:23.712 --> 24:25.297
Yes, this is Yoo Meri.

24:25.673 --> 24:27.675
-[Philnyun] It's me.
-Pardon?

24:28.092 --> 24:29.343
Wooju's grandma.

24:30.135 --> 24:31.220
[gasps]

24:32.054 --> 24:33.597
Hello, Chairwoman.

24:34.306 --> 24:36.100
I'm being discharged today.

24:36.892 --> 24:40.229
So, sometime next week,
let's meet at home.

24:40.938 --> 24:42.940
Oh, I'm always free.

24:43.816 --> 24:46.735
I'll come by
if you call me when you're free.

24:46.819 --> 24:48.404
Yes, thank you.

24:48.487 --> 24:50.030
Goodbye, ma'am.

24:50.114 --> 24:51.490
[♪ whimsical music playing]

24:52.491 --> 24:53.534
[line disconnects]

24:53.617 --> 24:56.036
Was that a call from the chairwoman?

24:56.495 --> 24:58.330
-Yeah.
-[shrieks]

24:58.914 --> 25:00.249
[exclaims excitedly]

25:00.624 --> 25:02.584
-That startled me.
-[chuckles excitedly]

25:04.086 --> 25:05.504
That was such a surprise.

25:05.587 --> 25:07.089
[Wonseok vocalizing]

25:08.924 --> 25:10.843
I heard that the chairwoman
is getting discharged.

25:10.926 --> 25:13.303
-I wonder if she'll start work right away.
-[inhales sharply]

25:13.595 --> 25:15.431
I think that'd be a bit difficult

25:15.514 --> 25:17.766
since she'll need
to take it easy for a while.

25:17.850 --> 25:19.059
Also, considering her age.

25:19.143 --> 25:22.187
Then the acting chairman
will be Mr. Kim, right?

25:22.688 --> 25:24.064
Since Director Jang isn't here.

25:24.148 --> 25:25.733
[inhales sharply]

25:25.816 --> 25:26.942
That's probable.

25:27.026 --> 25:28.235
[sighs wearily]

25:28.318 --> 25:30.362
-Oh, no.
-Why?

25:30.696 --> 25:33.532
Don't you think I've been
a bit rude to Ms. Yoo recently?

25:34.324 --> 25:35.409
[exclaims]

25:35.492 --> 25:36.493
Perhaps...

25:37.703 --> 25:38.746
[sighs softly]

25:39.121 --> 25:40.873
-...just a little.
-[sighs]

25:40.956 --> 25:43.500
I bet I'm on her bad side now.

25:43.584 --> 25:47.129
[chuckles] If you are,
then what about Ms. Oh?

25:47.212 --> 25:48.547
-[chuckling]
-What about me?

25:48.630 --> 25:49.673
[both gasp]

25:50.299 --> 25:51.383
Nothing.

25:51.675 --> 25:53.802
You must have a lot of free time, Sejung,

25:53.886 --> 25:55.554
worrying about such things.

25:56.138 --> 25:58.724
It's not like Ms. Yoo
is getting married right now.

25:58.807 --> 26:00.434
Focus on work.

26:03.228 --> 26:07.316
Also, you never really know with couples
until they walk down the aisle.

26:08.317 --> 26:09.735
Oh, good morning, Ms. Yoo.

26:09.818 --> 26:11.070
[♪ whimsical music playing]

26:11.820 --> 26:13.113
[Ms. Oh chuckles softly]

26:13.989 --> 26:15.157
Here. [chuckles softly]

26:15.783 --> 26:16.950
[Wonseok] Thank you.

26:17.034 --> 26:18.660
You really didn't need to.

26:18.744 --> 26:19.912
Seriously.

26:19.995 --> 26:22.706
We should. It's give and take.

26:22.790 --> 26:23.791
[Ms. Oh] "Give and take"?

26:24.124 --> 26:25.250
We're a family, aren't we?

26:25.334 --> 26:26.668
You're upsetting me now.

26:28.128 --> 26:29.129
Come sit.

26:29.588 --> 26:30.672
Thank you.

26:35.260 --> 26:37.304
You heard that Chairwoman
has been discharged, right?

26:37.387 --> 26:39.223
-Yes.
-She's going to visit her soon.

26:39.556 --> 26:40.641
Is that so?

26:40.724 --> 26:41.934
[exclaiming thoughtfully]

26:42.017 --> 26:44.645
Then I should give you some advice.

26:45.687 --> 26:47.523
Are you good at omok?

26:48.065 --> 26:49.149
Omok?

26:49.691 --> 26:52.194
-A bit.
-She's really good at it.

26:52.277 --> 26:54.071
She even wins against the computer.

26:54.154 --> 26:56.240
-She's the Lee Sedol of omok.
-[exclaims dismissively]

26:56.323 --> 26:57.324
[Ms. Oh] Really?

26:57.407 --> 26:59.952
The chairwoman is also the queen of omok.

27:00.661 --> 27:01.995
She almost never loses.

27:02.663 --> 27:03.872
[exclaims in amazement]

27:03.956 --> 27:05.791
Then should I go play omok with her?

27:05.874 --> 27:07.417
[Ms. Oh] No.

27:07.835 --> 27:10.212
What will you do if you win against her?

27:11.380 --> 27:12.840
I think it was about ten years ago.

27:12.923 --> 27:15.634
A factory manager beat her once,

27:15.717 --> 27:17.427
and he had a rough week after that.

27:17.511 --> 27:20.222
She wouldn't even look him in the eye
for a whole week.

27:21.598 --> 27:23.517
He was totally out of her favor.

27:24.226 --> 27:26.520
Then, I shouldn't win.

27:26.603 --> 27:27.855
That's right.

27:27.938 --> 27:29.773
This is really important advice.

27:29.857 --> 27:31.483
No one would've told you but me.

27:31.900 --> 27:33.068
Thank you.

27:33.151 --> 27:35.028
Do you have any other advice?

27:35.112 --> 27:36.196
SAUNA

27:36.280 --> 27:38.073
-[sighs] Jinhwa.
-Yes?

27:38.156 --> 27:40.576
-What should we have for dinner?
-[hums thoughtfully]

27:40.659 --> 27:42.870
How about Szechuan-style
sweet and sour pork?

27:42.953 --> 27:45.706
I'll make it for you.
We just need to buy pork.

27:45.789 --> 27:49.251
Hey, look at you all excited
about the cooking school these days.

27:49.334 --> 27:52.754
I think that's where my hidden talent is.

27:52.838 --> 27:53.881
[imitates knife chopping]

27:53.964 --> 27:55.090
-[exclaims]
-[chuckles]

27:55.173 --> 27:57.718
[chuckles] I can't even be bothered
to shop for groceries.

27:57.801 --> 27:58.886
Let's just eat out.

27:58.969 --> 28:00.637
Call Wooju out.

28:00.721 --> 28:03.640
Geez, I was going to show off my skills.

28:05.475 --> 28:06.602
[exclaims quizzically]

28:06.685 --> 28:07.728
Mom.

28:08.854 --> 28:09.938
Isn't that Wooju?

28:10.647 --> 28:12.399
[Eunsook] Hey, it is.

28:13.275 --> 28:14.526
That's a woman in front of him.

28:15.444 --> 28:16.486
Who is that?

28:18.530 --> 28:20.908
I'm Lee Soyeong,
a reporter from Junghan Magazine.

28:20.991 --> 28:23.327
I saw that you
canceled the press conference.

28:23.410 --> 28:25.579
Could you tell me about it?

28:26.288 --> 28:28.540
[chief officer] The moment
our department store is mentioned,

28:28.624 --> 28:30.792
we'll estimate the business loss
caused by defamation

28:30.876 --> 28:32.044
and file a claim for damages.

28:32.127 --> 28:33.170
[gulps]

28:33.378 --> 28:34.379
It's nothing.

28:34.463 --> 28:36.089
I had it all wrong.

28:37.257 --> 28:40.052
I'm sorry for all the trouble I've caused.

28:48.852 --> 28:49.853
[Soyeong] Excuse me.

28:50.312 --> 28:51.313
Please wait.

28:52.272 --> 28:53.815
If you called for a press conference,

28:53.899 --> 28:55.525
you must've had some kind of proof

28:55.609 --> 28:57.569
that the Myungsoondang's heir
committed fraud.

28:59.029 --> 29:01.031
I'd prefer it
if you stopped asking me about it.

29:03.075 --> 29:04.076
Excuse me.

29:05.035 --> 29:06.036
Here.

29:06.954 --> 29:09.665
If you ever change your mind,
please call me.

29:18.382 --> 29:19.424
[Wooju sighs softly]

29:21.718 --> 29:22.886
[♪ whimsical music playing]

29:22.970 --> 29:24.346
[Eunsook] A press conference?

29:24.930 --> 29:26.807
Who is the heir of Myungsoondang?

29:27.933 --> 29:29.267
Do you know him?

29:29.351 --> 29:31.019
No, how would I know someone like that?

29:32.020 --> 29:33.313
The reporter came to me by mistake.

29:33.397 --> 29:34.731
Tell me now.

29:34.815 --> 29:35.816
Tell us.

29:35.899 --> 29:38.610
Otherwise, I'm going to ask her directly.

29:46.994 --> 29:49.079
[Jinhwa] Myungsoondang's Kim Wooju...

29:49.871 --> 29:50.872
[gasps]

29:51.748 --> 29:53.000
That's right.

29:53.083 --> 29:54.668
This is the guy.

29:54.751 --> 29:56.503
He was in Wooju's hospital room.

29:57.045 --> 29:58.213
And at that store, too.

29:58.296 --> 29:59.881
We saw him there with Meri.

29:59.965 --> 30:01.842
-[gasps]
-It's him, right?

30:03.969 --> 30:04.970
Oh, my.

30:05.470 --> 30:06.805
Oh, my gosh.

30:06.888 --> 30:09.516
-[sighs]
-Meri really hit the jackpot.

30:09.599 --> 30:11.768
How is she marrying
into such a rich family?

30:12.227 --> 30:13.395
But seriously,

30:13.979 --> 30:15.939
look at this guy.

30:16.023 --> 30:18.275
He looks so classy.

30:18.775 --> 30:22.070
Mom, I'm more envious
of how handsome he is

30:22.154 --> 30:23.697
than the fact that she's marrying rich.

30:23.780 --> 30:24.906
Oh, I could just...

30:26.575 --> 30:28.035
[softly] You startled me.

30:28.118 --> 30:29.327
[laughing]

30:32.456 --> 30:34.750
This is unbelievable.

30:36.084 --> 30:37.502
-Hey.
-Yeah?

30:37.586 --> 30:38.587
His family

30:39.296 --> 30:40.839
is from Myungsoondang, right?

30:44.259 --> 30:48.346
You already seem happy at the thought
of getting a granddaughter-in-law.

30:48.430 --> 30:51.058
I'm just happy to get rid of Wooju.

30:51.141 --> 30:52.517
[chuckles softly]

30:53.060 --> 30:54.311
Still, it's a relief

30:54.686 --> 30:57.189
that I get to see him
getting married before I die.

30:58.523 --> 31:00.734
Perhaps that's why Wooju's dad woke me up.

31:03.403 --> 31:05.280
You should live to see
your great-grandchild.

31:06.239 --> 31:07.783
Don't say that.

31:08.575 --> 31:10.577
What if they ask me to babysit?

31:11.161 --> 31:14.873
I'm old-fashioned, so I can't pamper kids
the way moms do these days.

31:15.123 --> 31:16.416
[chuckles]

31:17.459 --> 31:18.919
You look beautiful today, as always.

31:19.002 --> 31:20.128
[both chuckle]

31:20.879 --> 31:22.839
There's still time, please rest a bit.

31:22.923 --> 31:23.965
[chuckles softly]

31:28.804 --> 31:30.931
Because you told me not to,

31:31.014 --> 31:34.392
I haven't looked
into Ms. Yoo Meri's personal background.

31:35.185 --> 31:36.269
But...

31:38.271 --> 31:39.689
are you sure about this?

31:41.024 --> 31:42.943
I met her a couple of times.

31:43.026 --> 31:44.569
She seemed like a good person.

31:45.445 --> 31:46.738
I haven't lost my touch yet.

31:48.073 --> 31:49.449
Yes, ma'am. [chuckles softly]

31:49.908 --> 31:51.409
Ask them where they are.

31:51.493 --> 31:52.661
Yes, ma'am.

31:57.207 --> 31:58.291
[sighs softly]

31:58.375 --> 31:59.376
Yes.

32:00.210 --> 32:02.170
We're at the flower shop
in front of the house.

32:03.088 --> 32:04.256
We'll be there soon.

32:04.589 --> 32:05.590
Okay.

32:05.882 --> 32:06.925
[line disconnects]

32:07.008 --> 32:09.928
I think Grandma is in a hurry to meet you.

32:10.011 --> 32:11.138
Do I look okay today?

32:11.680 --> 32:12.722
You look beautiful.

32:12.806 --> 32:14.641
Let's go. [giggles]

32:16.810 --> 32:18.436
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

32:31.783 --> 32:33.285
[doorbell chiming]

32:36.371 --> 32:37.831
[doorbell chiming]

32:38.415 --> 32:39.541
That must be them.

32:40.000 --> 32:41.960
-Okay, I'll go and let them in.
-Sure.

32:44.004 --> 32:45.463
[Eunsook gasps in awe]

32:52.596 --> 32:54.973
Mom, this house is... [scoffs]

32:55.056 --> 32:57.017
You said you had something to tell me

32:58.101 --> 32:59.644
about Ms. Yoo Meri.

33:00.020 --> 33:01.021
I do.

33:01.813 --> 33:03.440
Let me introduce myself first.

33:04.858 --> 33:05.859
I am

33:06.484 --> 33:11.656
the ex-mother-in-law of Meri,
who is currently dating your grandson.

33:11.740 --> 33:12.991
And I'm her ex-sister-in-law.

33:13.783 --> 33:14.784
Mother-in-law?

33:16.244 --> 33:17.245
Don't tell me...

33:17.704 --> 33:19.748
Didn't you know she's a divorcée?

33:19.831 --> 33:21.374
[♪ tense music playing]

33:21.458 --> 33:22.459
See?

33:22.542 --> 33:24.753
She was about to ruin another man's life.

33:25.378 --> 33:26.379
Gosh.

33:26.796 --> 33:29.883
Please, take your time
and tell me what you mean.

33:29.966 --> 33:31.134
Yes, ma'am.

33:31.218 --> 33:33.637
-That girl, Meri...
-That girl...

33:43.897 --> 33:45.232
[phone vibrating]

33:46.858 --> 33:47.859
Yes, we've arrived.

33:49.486 --> 33:50.487
Pardon?

33:50.570 --> 33:52.822
She asked to see you alone.

33:55.116 --> 33:57.035
What? All of a sudden...

34:00.622 --> 34:01.790
Oh, okay.

34:03.375 --> 34:04.376
I'm sorry.

34:04.459 --> 34:06.461
I don't think you can meet Grandma today.

34:06.544 --> 34:09.089
She says she's suddenly not feeling well.

34:09.172 --> 34:10.590
Oh, really?

34:10.674 --> 34:12.384
Is she very sick?

34:12.467 --> 34:14.261
Well, I'm not so sure.

34:14.886 --> 34:16.429
I'll have to go see her.

34:16.513 --> 34:18.348
Do you mind waiting in the car?

34:18.431 --> 34:21.059
No, don't worry about me, and go in.

34:24.271 --> 34:25.272
Go on.

34:40.120 --> 34:41.121
I'll get going.

34:49.296 --> 34:51.548
[door opens, closes]

34:52.882 --> 34:53.883
What's...

34:53.967 --> 34:55.302
Is Ms. Yoo Meri

34:56.720 --> 34:57.721
divorced?

34:57.804 --> 34:59.222
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

35:03.268 --> 35:04.561
[Kim Wooju clears throat]

35:04.644 --> 35:07.522
We were going to tell you about that
along with everything else.

35:07.606 --> 35:08.773
"Everything else"?

35:10.108 --> 35:12.694
I guess there's more
that I'd be surprised about.

35:30.629 --> 35:32.380
[♪ soft, poignant music playing]

35:33.214 --> 35:34.507
Meri... [breath trembling]

35:35.216 --> 35:37.093
Can I ask you to think over this again?

35:37.177 --> 35:38.845
I don't have any money.

35:38.928 --> 35:41.473
[crying] Could you please talk to Beauté

35:42.682 --> 35:44.684
and ask them to drop the lawsuit?

35:44.768 --> 35:47.103
Why did you have to take things this far?

35:47.187 --> 35:49.356
What made you take it this far?

35:52.275 --> 35:55.487
Seeing you broken
and falling apart like this

35:55.570 --> 35:57.072
doesn't make me happy

35:58.573 --> 35:59.616
or satisfied.

35:59.699 --> 36:00.742
[sobbing]

36:02.911 --> 36:05.372
Let's forget that you hurt me

36:06.581 --> 36:08.208
and your hatred toward me.

36:09.334 --> 36:11.252
Let's forget it all...

36:12.087 --> 36:14.297
and just keep the good memories.

36:14.839 --> 36:15.965
[sighs softly]

36:18.176 --> 36:19.761
Maybe I'm being punished.

36:23.598 --> 36:26.685
All the good days are behind me...

36:29.396 --> 36:31.439
and I lost a good woman like Meri.

36:33.900 --> 36:35.026
[chuckles wistfully]

36:36.069 --> 36:37.821
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

36:58.675 --> 36:59.676
Meri,

37:00.677 --> 37:01.678
I'm sorry.

37:06.683 --> 37:07.851
I know it's late,

37:10.103 --> 37:11.229
but I really mean it.

37:12.147 --> 37:13.314
I'm really sorry.

37:21.030 --> 37:22.949
I want you to be happy, too.

37:25.201 --> 37:26.202
SISTER

37:28.329 --> 37:29.330
[sighs wearily]

37:32.041 --> 37:33.042
What?

37:36.212 --> 37:37.338
What am I doing?

37:39.340 --> 37:40.341
Meri?

37:41.926 --> 37:43.636
Why would she call me?

37:47.390 --> 37:48.391
What?

37:49.017 --> 37:50.101
You went where?

37:50.685 --> 37:51.853
[breath trembling]

37:52.562 --> 37:53.938
Why would you do that?

37:54.439 --> 37:56.357
Stop it already.

37:56.441 --> 38:00.028
[yelling] You and Mom both,
please stop it already!

38:00.195 --> 38:02.363
-[line disconnects]
-[sobbing] Oh, gosh...

38:08.787 --> 38:11.372
CEO YOO MERI

38:13.374 --> 38:14.459
[mouse clicks]

38:15.668 --> 38:16.669
[phone pings]

38:19.214 --> 38:20.548
KIM WOOJU

38:20.632 --> 38:21.716
[Wooju] Meri.

38:21.800 --> 38:24.511
It looks like my mom
went to see Mr. Kim's grandma.

38:24.594 --> 38:26.262
I think she said some things about you.

38:26.346 --> 38:27.680
I'm really sorry.

38:27.764 --> 38:28.807
I apologize on her behalf.

38:30.767 --> 38:32.477
[♪ melancholy music playing]

38:32.852 --> 38:33.978
I'm sorry.

38:34.062 --> 38:35.647
I don't think you can meet Grandma today.

38:35.730 --> 38:38.024
She says she's suddenly not feeling well.

38:38.942 --> 38:40.193
[sighs wearily]

38:41.361 --> 38:42.946
So, that's what happened.

38:47.951 --> 38:49.035
[sighs softly]

38:59.212 --> 39:00.213
[Philnyun] What?

39:00.296 --> 39:02.006
She even committed fraud?

39:05.927 --> 39:07.136
[phone vibrating]

39:10.390 --> 39:12.433
MYUNGSOON

39:12.725 --> 39:13.810
[clears throat]

39:14.227 --> 39:15.812
-Hello.
-Hi.

39:15.895 --> 39:18.481
I was just wondering
how Chairwoman is doing.

39:19.190 --> 39:21.734
Oh, it wasn't something serious.

39:21.818 --> 39:23.945
She said she was
just not feeling her best.

39:24.654 --> 39:25.655
I see.

39:26.406 --> 39:28.908
Didn't she say anything else?

39:29.951 --> 39:30.952
No.

39:32.871 --> 39:33.997
Did you get home safely?

39:34.664 --> 39:35.999
I'm on my way now.

39:36.666 --> 39:40.420
I'll rearrange the meeting
for some other time when there's a chance.

39:41.087 --> 39:42.422
-For the time being...
-About that.

39:42.505 --> 39:44.215
Don't worry about it too much.

39:44.299 --> 39:45.758
It's not urgent.

39:46.718 --> 39:47.719
Yes.

39:49.178 --> 39:50.388
Good night.

39:52.557 --> 39:53.558
[line disconnects]

39:58.479 --> 39:59.731
[sighs wearily]

40:10.575 --> 40:11.743
[sighs wearily]

40:16.998 --> 40:18.166
[phone vibrating]

40:18.875 --> 40:20.585
MOM

40:24.756 --> 40:26.090
No, that one.

40:26.174 --> 40:28.301
-They're all the same.
-Mom.

40:28.384 --> 40:29.469
Hey, sweetie.

40:30.303 --> 40:34.057
Didn't you say that you were
going to meet his grandma?

40:34.140 --> 40:37.268
Why didn't you call
to tell me how it went?

40:37.352 --> 40:39.395
I've been waiting forever.

40:40.605 --> 40:43.316
-[whispering indistinctly]
-[exclaims]

40:44.984 --> 40:45.985
You didn't meet her?

40:47.946 --> 40:49.781
[sighs softly] Well...

40:51.908 --> 40:53.159
What?

40:57.705 --> 41:00.291
Mom, are you sure about this?

41:00.375 --> 41:01.376
My gosh.

41:02.001 --> 41:03.044
It doesn't matter

41:03.461 --> 41:06.506
whether I'm sure or not, okay?

41:08.800 --> 41:11.135
I'm going to settle this once and for all.

41:12.095 --> 41:13.763
Okay, I get it. [in English] Calm down.

41:14.138 --> 41:15.431
Calm down.

41:15.515 --> 41:16.516
[breathing heavily]

41:18.351 --> 41:19.852
[in Korean] Mom, isn't that them?

41:19.936 --> 41:21.104
-Where?
-There.

41:21.187 --> 41:23.356
[gasps] Gosh, yes.

41:23.690 --> 41:25.733
Right, wait a minute.

41:25.817 --> 41:26.818
Wait.

41:27.402 --> 41:29.362
-[in English] Stop. [grunts]
-[tires screech]

41:32.240 --> 41:33.408
[in Korean] Hey!

41:33.491 --> 41:35.159
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

41:37.412 --> 41:39.038
Oh, my gosh. Who are you?

41:39.122 --> 41:41.416
Oh, my. [stutters] Meri's mother!

41:41.499 --> 41:44.627
-Let's end this together!
-No, stop!

41:44.711 --> 41:46.504
I'll make you pay for everything

41:46.587 --> 41:49.590
-Ms. Oh!
-you did to my daughter!

41:49.674 --> 41:52.510
What's happening? Jinhwa!

41:52.593 --> 41:54.929
-Let's end this together!
-Ms. Oh!

41:55.221 --> 41:59.308
I'm going to make you pay
for what you did to my daughter!

41:59.392 --> 42:01.310
-Why are you...
-Ms. Oh!

42:01.394 --> 42:02.854
[Jinhwa] Stop this!

42:03.604 --> 42:07.025
-[screams] Hey!
-How dare you mess with my sister?

42:07.108 --> 42:09.610
-Who's this? Let me go.
-How dare you?

42:11.154 --> 42:12.155
Hey!

42:12.238 --> 42:13.239
[screams]

42:15.408 --> 42:16.868
[all screaming, grunting]

42:19.954 --> 42:21.748
[Eunsook] Please, help.

42:21.831 --> 42:24.125
-[Youngsook] To my daughter...
-Please, help me.

42:24.208 --> 42:25.418
-Ms. Oh!
-You're so dead.

42:26.919 --> 42:29.839
[Jinhwa] Please, help me!

42:48.816 --> 42:50.026
[sighs wearily]

42:56.991 --> 42:58.159
You're here early.

42:58.993 --> 42:59.994
[exclaims quizzically]

43:00.661 --> 43:01.746
What?

43:01.829 --> 43:03.289
Isn't today your trial?

43:03.372 --> 43:04.373
[chuckles softly]

43:04.791 --> 43:09.170
I came in case you were upset
about a guy standing you up again.

43:09.253 --> 43:10.254
What?

43:11.130 --> 43:12.131
What is it?

43:12.215 --> 43:15.676
Do you think I'm drowning my sorrows
because a guy stood me up?

43:15.760 --> 43:16.803
I'm not.

43:19.597 --> 43:21.224
Are you trying to flirt with me?

43:21.307 --> 43:22.975
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

43:24.268 --> 43:26.187
Are you trying to flirt with me?

43:27.939 --> 43:29.023
[sighs deeply]

43:30.942 --> 43:33.027
Someone comforted me recently.

43:34.278 --> 43:37.990
I realized that money
isn't everything in this world.

43:39.075 --> 43:40.201
Thanks to that person,

43:40.827 --> 43:42.870
I feel so much at ease now.

43:43.621 --> 43:46.040
I'm not sure who that person is,

43:46.124 --> 43:48.584
but they must be a really great person.

43:50.044 --> 43:51.921
Anyway, I like your attitude now.

43:52.630 --> 43:53.631
[in English] Respect.

43:55.383 --> 43:56.384
[in English] Respect

43:57.343 --> 43:58.719
[both chuckle]

44:04.767 --> 44:05.852
[in Korean] Your trial...

44:06.644 --> 44:08.104
I hope it goes well.

44:18.156 --> 44:19.448
[in Korean] I'll get going first.

44:23.286 --> 44:24.620
Wait for me!

44:24.704 --> 44:26.080
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

44:32.753 --> 44:36.007
By the way,
why did you ask me for such a favor?

44:36.841 --> 44:38.342
Because I had no one to ask.

44:38.426 --> 44:40.469
Wait, is that really it?

44:42.972 --> 44:44.140
You can say no.

44:44.223 --> 44:46.058
That's not what I'm saying.

44:46.142 --> 44:47.852
I'm just curious.

44:47.935 --> 44:49.312
Like, when do I start?

44:49.395 --> 44:51.939
This comes with a lot
of responsibility, doesn't it?

44:52.565 --> 44:53.900
Wait for me!

44:53.983 --> 44:55.318
[Sanghyeon] Hurry up!

44:55.401 --> 44:57.069
[Jingyeong] Oh, seriously.

44:57.153 --> 44:58.404
You're too fast.

45:01.657 --> 45:03.242
[♪ soft jazz music playing in background]

45:04.410 --> 45:07.580
[Meri] We thought everything
would go smoothly,

45:08.706 --> 45:12.418
but as we each carried
our own unspoken worries,

45:12.919 --> 45:16.172
life got busier, and we drifted apart.

45:20.927 --> 45:23.304
Did I tell you
that Eungsoo quit the company?

45:23.721 --> 45:25.139
No, you mean Mr. Jang?

45:26.557 --> 45:29.101
He suddenly wants to become
an esports team owner.

45:29.185 --> 45:32.605
He wanted to chase his passion,
so he handed in his resignation last week.

45:32.980 --> 45:33.981
I see.

45:34.065 --> 45:36.192
-I didn't know he liked games.
-He does.

45:36.567 --> 45:40.196
He's busy these days
scouting professional gamers.

45:40.279 --> 45:42.907
And it makes me busy, too,
trying to fill in for him.

45:49.288 --> 45:52.625
You also seemed busy,
seeing how you call less.

45:53.376 --> 45:54.418
[hesitates]

45:54.502 --> 45:56.420
It's because of the meetings.

45:57.088 --> 45:58.631
With the new project,

45:58.714 --> 46:01.801
it's been a bit hectic
going back and forth from Daejeon.

46:01.884 --> 46:04.303
Oh, I see.

46:09.517 --> 46:11.686
MADAM KO

46:15.147 --> 46:16.315
[phone vibrating]

46:16.816 --> 46:18.234
Can you give me a minute?

46:43.592 --> 46:45.261
I'd like to pay, please.

46:50.975 --> 46:52.018
[card reader beeps]

46:52.101 --> 46:54.020
Please sign here.

46:56.897 --> 46:58.190
-[printer whirring]
-[receipt rips]

46:59.608 --> 47:01.277
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

47:02.486 --> 47:05.156
[Kim Wooju] No, I told you already.

47:05.239 --> 47:08.492
Unlike how you think...

47:09.118 --> 47:10.369
No, I mean...

47:11.620 --> 47:12.621
[sighs wearily]

47:13.581 --> 47:15.958
Grandma, can you please reconsider?

47:17.460 --> 47:19.420
[♪ melancholy music playing]

47:26.344 --> 47:28.262
I'm sorry. I have to get home.

47:28.346 --> 47:30.473
It's fine. Your grandma is asking for you.

47:30.556 --> 47:31.766
You should get going.

47:32.141 --> 47:33.309
[engine starts]

48:19.146 --> 48:20.689
Since everyone is here,

48:22.608 --> 48:24.026
I'll tell you my decisions.

48:26.237 --> 48:28.114
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

48:39.458 --> 48:40.626
[sighs softly]

48:42.128 --> 48:44.755
Grandma, can you please reconsider?

48:45.381 --> 48:47.091
[sighs wearily] No, I mean...

48:48.175 --> 48:49.385
[phone vibrating]

48:53.848 --> 48:55.391
MYUNGSIK

48:57.977 --> 48:58.978
Hi.

48:59.520 --> 49:00.521
[Kim Wooju] Where are you?

49:02.106 --> 49:03.899
I'm at the playground
in front of my house.

49:04.525 --> 49:07.486
I came out for fresh air
since the wind is nice.

49:07.570 --> 49:08.779
"Came out for fresh air"?

49:08.863 --> 49:10.406
I bet you were out this whole time.

49:10.865 --> 49:11.866
Pardon?

49:11.949 --> 49:14.869
You haven't even changed.
What are you doing all alone at this hour?

49:25.504 --> 49:26.547
[line disconnects]

49:27.214 --> 49:28.299
Wooju.

49:35.514 --> 49:38.476
I was on my way to your place to see you.

49:38.559 --> 49:41.687
And I saw you just sitting here,

49:41.770 --> 49:44.148
glowing under the lights
with that stunning beauty.

49:45.816 --> 49:47.568
What did your grandma say?

49:48.986 --> 49:51.947
I'm sure she called you in
because she had something to say.

49:52.031 --> 49:53.073
[hesitates]

49:54.992 --> 49:56.076
[clears throat]

49:57.661 --> 49:59.413
She's against us, right?

49:59.997 --> 50:00.998
What?

50:01.081 --> 50:04.251
Wooju's mom paid a visit to your grandma.

50:05.628 --> 50:07.546
I think I know what she told her.

50:10.841 --> 50:12.718
I'm fine,

50:12.801 --> 50:14.762
so don't struggle in between.

50:15.054 --> 50:16.430
I'm not struggling.

50:18.140 --> 50:19.391
I heard you

50:19.934 --> 50:22.144
talking to your grandma at the restaurant.

50:24.313 --> 50:25.606
[exclaims in realization]

50:26.273 --> 50:27.399
[sighs wearily]

50:27.483 --> 50:30.152
Grandma, can you please reconsider?

50:33.239 --> 50:36.825
[chuckles softly]
I'm very grateful for the offer,

50:36.909 --> 50:39.787
but I'm not ready
to take over the company yet.

50:40.538 --> 50:43.082
How about we hire a professional manager?

50:43.749 --> 50:45.251
You should've stayed to hear the rest.

50:45.668 --> 50:49.421
Grandma wants me to take over the company.

50:49.505 --> 50:51.173
-What?
-Geez.

50:51.257 --> 50:52.716
You went off in your own head again.

50:54.635 --> 50:58.264
Well, she didn't ask
to see me again, so...

50:58.347 --> 51:01.183
About that, she said
she needs a bit more time.

51:02.017 --> 51:03.060
[acknowledges]

51:03.811 --> 51:04.812
What?

51:05.521 --> 51:07.106
She even committed fraud?

51:07.189 --> 51:10.067
But you said it yourself,

51:10.150 --> 51:11.819
anyone can make mistakes.

51:12.236 --> 51:14.989
What matters is having the heart
and the will to make things right.

51:15.739 --> 51:16.824
[sighs in exasperation]

51:18.450 --> 51:19.493
Grandma...

51:19.577 --> 51:20.661
I have a headache.

51:21.453 --> 51:22.830
Let me think about it.

51:24.415 --> 51:27.084
[Kim Wooju] Do you know how anxious
I've been, waiting for her permission?

51:27.543 --> 51:28.544
[sighs softly]

51:29.003 --> 51:30.879
You should've told me.

51:31.255 --> 51:32.339
[chuckles softly]

51:33.340 --> 51:34.925
Do you know why she called me in today?

51:42.516 --> 51:43.726
She gave me this.

51:45.144 --> 51:47.104
She said, you can earn money whenever,

51:47.187 --> 51:49.189
eat delicious food whenever,

51:49.732 --> 51:51.609
and travel whenever.

51:53.819 --> 51:55.529
But there's a time for a proposal.

51:57.990 --> 52:01.035
She also said, if I ever meet someone
I want to spend the rest of my life with,

52:01.118 --> 52:02.661
I shouldn't lose her.

52:02.745 --> 52:04.413
[♪ gentle, dreamy music playing]

52:20.888 --> 52:21.889
Meri.

52:25.684 --> 52:27.728
Would you marry me?

52:35.027 --> 52:37.071
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

52:43.952 --> 52:44.953
Meri?

52:45.621 --> 52:46.622
Yes.

52:46.705 --> 52:47.956
[chuckles in relief]

52:49.124 --> 52:50.250
[chuckles softly]

52:51.418 --> 52:52.586
[clears throat] Well,

52:53.253 --> 52:56.006
someone said I shouldn't answer too fast.

52:57.383 --> 52:59.885
[chuckling] I was counting to ten,
but I failed.

53:00.969 --> 53:02.346
-[chuckles]
-[Meri sniffles]

53:18.320 --> 53:20.531
-[sniffles]
-[sighs contentedly]

53:49.977 --> 53:51.145
[sighs contentedly]

53:56.150 --> 53:57.484
[birds chirping]

54:07.244 --> 54:09.580
I've made many mistakes,

54:09.663 --> 54:12.666
but thank you
for forgiving me and accepting me.

54:12.750 --> 54:14.001
Sure.

54:14.084 --> 54:16.378
I hope you learned a lot from this.

54:17.546 --> 54:19.298
Make sure to keep it in your mind.

54:20.424 --> 54:21.592
I'll keep it in mind.

54:21.675 --> 54:23.302
I will, too.

54:23.385 --> 54:24.845
Mom! [chuckles]

54:25.637 --> 54:27.264
I heard Wooju's fiancée is coming.

54:27.347 --> 54:29.141
Mom, look to your left.

54:29.725 --> 54:30.726
She's here.

54:30.809 --> 54:32.186
Nice to meet you, Ms. Kim.

54:32.269 --> 54:33.604
My name is Yoo Meri.

54:33.687 --> 54:34.688
Hi, I'm...

54:37.107 --> 54:38.233
Wooju's aunt.

54:38.859 --> 54:40.527
This is his cousin.

54:40.611 --> 54:41.695
Say hi.

54:41.779 --> 54:44.615
We already know each other.
Aren't I right?

54:44.698 --> 54:46.825
-Have you been well?
-Yes.

54:46.909 --> 54:48.660
[Eungsoo and Miyeon chuckle]

54:48.994 --> 54:50.078
[Miyeon] You know,

54:51.038 --> 54:53.457
she resembles her mother a lot.

54:53.540 --> 54:55.876
Yeah, she does. She also looks fierce.

54:55.959 --> 54:57.461
-Yeah.
-Right?

54:57.544 --> 54:59.755
Have you seen my mother?

54:59.838 --> 55:01.715
We visited Yeosu, actually.

55:01.798 --> 55:04.760
We went there ourselves
on Grandma's order.

55:04.843 --> 55:06.136
It was quite far.

55:06.720 --> 55:08.263
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

55:10.224 --> 55:14.019
YOUNGSOOK'S RESTAURANT

55:25.072 --> 55:28.158
[exclaims contentedly]
How about this rolled omelet?

55:28.575 --> 55:29.701
Oh, my.

55:29.785 --> 55:30.786
[chuckles]

55:32.704 --> 55:35.040
[Eungsoo slurping loudly,
hums in satisfaction]

55:36.250 --> 55:38.168
This place is delicious.

55:39.253 --> 55:40.587
Mom, try it.

55:40.671 --> 55:42.381
-[Miyeon] Stop eating.
-[Eungsoo] Just try it.

55:42.464 --> 55:44.550
Just put it in your mouth.

55:44.633 --> 55:46.718
-[Eungsoo] Okay.
-You must be from Seoul.

55:47.678 --> 55:49.846
How did you know?

55:49.930 --> 55:51.473
You're not using dialect.

55:51.557 --> 55:53.225
I see. [chuckles softly]

55:54.560 --> 55:55.727
Are you the owner?

55:55.811 --> 55:58.313
-What?
-How's the business?

55:58.939 --> 56:00.607
How much is the profit?

56:00.691 --> 56:02.276
How would I know?

56:02.359 --> 56:04.653
I'm just a kitchen assistant.

56:04.736 --> 56:06.572
She's the owner.

56:10.075 --> 56:11.868
[♪ whimsical music playing]

56:13.954 --> 56:16.957
[Sunja] Geez, those were just testers.

56:17.040 --> 56:19.710
But he's making a meal out of it.

56:19.793 --> 56:21.795
If he eats like that
and doesn't buy anything,

56:21.878 --> 56:23.755
he's completely shameless.

56:24.256 --> 56:26.633
[clears throat] These... [chuckles]

56:26.717 --> 56:29.094
We're going to buy all of these.

56:29.177 --> 56:32.306
Could you pack these two up for us?

56:35.017 --> 56:37.519
[gasps] Oh, no.

56:37.603 --> 56:39.104
Wait.

56:39.646 --> 56:42.274
You can't take these, instead...

56:42.357 --> 56:44.359
Here, take this.

56:46.153 --> 56:49.281
Okay, then. But these cost the same,

56:49.865 --> 56:51.116
yet it's half the amount.

56:51.199 --> 56:53.577
Are you treating us differently
because we're not locals?

56:53.660 --> 56:56.496
-We're also in this business.
-It's not like that.

56:58.081 --> 57:01.084
-It's half the amount.
-Gosh, it's...

57:01.168 --> 57:03.253
-Hello.
-Oh, hey, Bohyeon.

57:03.337 --> 57:04.588
Wait a moment.

57:04.671 --> 57:05.964
Let's see.

57:06.048 --> 57:07.966
I packed all your favorites.

57:08.050 --> 57:09.384
Here.

57:09.468 --> 57:11.303
Enjoy it with your sister.

57:11.386 --> 57:12.929
Thank you.

57:20.228 --> 57:22.022
Thanks. Go on, now.

57:22.105 --> 57:23.607
Bye.

57:24.858 --> 57:27.611
[Sunja] Gosh, you're too generous.

57:27.694 --> 57:30.155
The business will fail at this rate.

57:30.238 --> 57:31.740
Nonsense.

57:32.407 --> 57:34.326
Oh, my. I'm sorry.

57:34.409 --> 57:37.788
Her mother died when she was younger,

57:37.871 --> 57:40.165
and her father's not home
as he's a fisherman.

57:40.248 --> 57:43.335
She's still a kid,
but she's got a younger one to look after.

57:43.418 --> 57:44.628
So, I feel bad for her.

57:44.711 --> 57:49.549
But she's too proud a girl
to take them for free.

57:49.633 --> 57:52.969
So, what else can I do
but give her a lot more?

57:53.053 --> 57:54.179
[chuckles]

57:54.429 --> 57:57.474
I'm not treating you differently,
so don't be upset.

57:57.557 --> 57:59.768
Oh, okay. [chuckles sheepishly]

57:59.851 --> 58:01.561
-So, you're from Seoul?
-Yes.

58:01.645 --> 58:04.606
Since you've been so gracious,
let's see...

58:05.232 --> 58:06.358
[grunts]

58:06.441 --> 58:07.693
Here.

58:07.776 --> 58:09.194
-Pollock pancakes?
-Pollock pancakes.

58:09.277 --> 58:11.029
-This is on the house.
-[chuckles]

58:11.113 --> 58:13.448
[chuckles] Our pollock pancakes
are amazing.

58:13.532 --> 58:14.658
[Eungsoo grunts]

58:16.076 --> 58:17.202
-[sighs]
-[grunts]

58:22.624 --> 58:23.667
[sighs softly]

58:25.460 --> 58:26.837
[line ringing]

58:27.587 --> 58:29.339
-[clears throat]
-Hi, Mom.

58:30.090 --> 58:32.801
I just saw Ms. Yoo Meri's mother,

58:32.884 --> 58:34.010
and I think...

58:35.011 --> 58:36.346
you'll like her.

58:36.430 --> 58:40.976
Like so, in relation to your marriage,
we played a very important role.

58:41.059 --> 58:42.561
-[laughs exultantly]
-[Miyeon chuckling]

58:44.271 --> 58:45.480
Thank you.

58:45.564 --> 58:48.984
Then I guess all that's left is
to set a date for the family meeting.

58:49.067 --> 58:50.986
About that...

58:52.028 --> 58:54.197
We're thinking of delaying our wedding.

58:55.615 --> 58:56.616
Why?

58:56.700 --> 58:59.536
Well, I just accepted the CEO position.

59:00.120 --> 59:02.748
So, I think it's only right
to focus more on the company right now.

59:03.623 --> 59:05.292
Meri also agreed to it.

59:05.959 --> 59:08.879
Yes, I also thought
that'd be for the best.

59:09.337 --> 59:10.338
[Philnyun] Is that right?

59:11.506 --> 59:14.009
If you both agree, then okay.

59:14.092 --> 59:15.469
I guess

59:16.344 --> 59:18.847
I'll just have to live longer.

59:18.930 --> 59:20.140
[all chuckle]

59:20.223 --> 59:22.017
[Miyeon] Oh, Mom...

59:22.851 --> 59:25.687
Son, this isn't the time for you to laugh.

59:25.771 --> 59:28.398
It's not too late yet.
How about I set you up?

59:28.482 --> 59:30.609
I'm a believer in natural encounters, Mom.

59:30.692 --> 59:32.944
I don't do blind dates, so no set-ups.

59:33.028 --> 59:34.446
It's not too late.

59:34.529 --> 59:36.907
Meri, do you have any friends
you can introduce?

59:36.990 --> 59:38.200
I have many.

59:38.283 --> 59:40.410
What do you think? Can you set him up?

59:40.494 --> 59:41.995
What kind of woman are you into?

59:42.078 --> 59:44.122
-Someone unlike Mom.
-[Miyeon] Someone like me.

59:45.290 --> 59:47.334
[Jingyeong] You guys are
going to live here from now on.

59:48.543 --> 59:51.171
This is also a place people stay in,

59:51.254 --> 59:53.006
so get used to it fast, okay?

59:53.924 --> 59:55.592
Especially you, Sweet.

59:56.301 --> 59:59.429
You've been looking so down lately,
just sleeping all the time.

01:00:01.348 --> 01:00:02.432
Or was it Sour?

01:00:04.392 --> 01:00:06.853
Oh, this is really confusing.

01:00:07.771 --> 01:00:09.314
Are you guys twins?

01:00:15.779 --> 01:00:18.949
How did your owner differentiate you two?

01:00:19.533 --> 01:00:21.034
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

01:00:22.577 --> 01:00:25.163
[sighs] Meal time.

01:00:46.393 --> 01:00:47.894
[sighs softly]

01:00:59.030 --> 01:01:00.532
[Jingyeong] Dear Mr. Baek.

01:01:01.074 --> 01:01:03.577
It's gotten quite cold
in the morning and at night.

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:07.289
Winter must be near,
judging by the days also getting shorter.

01:01:08.039 --> 01:01:09.374
You're doing well, right?

01:01:09.958 --> 01:01:13.253
It's been all hospital and home for me,

01:01:13.336 --> 01:01:16.548
but lately, I've really been
enjoying raising the turtles.

01:01:16.631 --> 01:01:19.551
I can't even tell
a turtle from a terrapin,

01:01:19.634 --> 01:01:22.429
but I've been turning into a turtle expert

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:24.681
from trying to tell
the twin-like Sweet and Sour apart,

01:01:25.432 --> 01:01:26.850
You said I just need to feed them

01:01:26.933 --> 01:01:29.519
and change their water from time to time.

01:01:29.603 --> 01:01:30.770
But guess what?

01:01:30.854 --> 01:01:32.731
I also have to check
if they're still alive

01:01:33.273 --> 01:01:35.942
because they're way too quiet.

01:01:37.193 --> 01:01:39.988
I think they're introverts,
taking after you.

01:01:40.071 --> 01:01:41.072
[chuckles]

01:01:44.492 --> 01:01:47.662
I'll be participating
in the Boston Marathon next spring.

01:01:47.746 --> 01:01:51.249
I'll complete it and send you
a proof photo at the Charles River.

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:52.584
Would you like to join me

01:01:52.667 --> 01:01:54.669
for the next November's
New York City Marathon?

01:01:54.753 --> 01:01:56.796
I can complete the course now.

01:01:56.880 --> 01:02:01.009
If you want to match my pace,
you'll have to train hard until then.

01:02:01.092 --> 01:02:03.345
I'll take good care of your turtles,

01:02:03.428 --> 01:02:06.973
so don't worry and stay healthy.

01:02:07.057 --> 01:02:08.558
BEFORE I KNEW YOU,
I GOT ALONG WITHOUT POETRY

01:02:08.642 --> 01:02:11.478
Like these turtles,
who are dependent on their strong shells,

01:02:11.561 --> 01:02:15.607
I hope you're growing stronger
through your days there.

01:02:16.399 --> 01:02:17.734
I'll write to you again.

01:02:27.077 --> 01:02:28.453
[sighs deeply]

01:02:36.628 --> 01:02:38.421
1 YEAR LATER

01:02:38.505 --> 01:02:41.132
[Sejung] An outdoor wedding?
It looks like it's going to rain.

01:02:41.216 --> 01:02:42.384
[Ms. Oh] Tell me about it.

01:02:42.884 --> 01:02:44.511
Why do I have to carry things like this?

01:02:45.470 --> 01:02:47.722
What's wrong with it?
The grass smells nice.

01:02:47.806 --> 01:02:50.433
Also, I always dreamed
of having an outdoor wedding.

01:02:50.517 --> 01:02:51.893
He's right.

01:02:51.977 --> 01:02:54.312
And they say you live happily
if it rains on your wedding day.

01:02:54.396 --> 01:02:55.605
So, I guess it's lucky.

01:02:55.689 --> 01:02:56.731
How lucky!

01:02:56.815 --> 01:02:58.274
Whatever.

01:02:59.609 --> 01:03:00.610
[screams]

01:03:00.694 --> 01:03:01.945
[Wonseok] What's wrong?

01:03:02.404 --> 01:03:03.405
[Ms. Oh] Wait...

01:03:04.489 --> 01:03:05.490
What's this?

01:03:05.573 --> 01:03:08.076
I can't believe this. These are new!

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:10.328
Oh, my clothes are new, too.

01:03:10.412 --> 01:03:11.705
[Wonseok] Me too.

01:03:11.788 --> 01:03:13.081
[Songhee] Oh, no...

01:03:13.164 --> 01:03:15.417
[Eungsoo] "Ms. Yoo Meri..."

01:03:15.500 --> 01:03:16.501
[Ms. Oh] My shoes...

01:03:16.584 --> 01:03:17.585
-Oh, hello.
-Hi.

01:03:17.669 --> 01:03:18.753
Oh, no. Are you hurt?

01:03:18.837 --> 01:03:20.422
No, it's just my heel.

01:03:20.505 --> 01:03:21.506
I see.

01:03:22.382 --> 01:03:24.509
-[Ms. Oh] No, not there.
-[Eungsoo] Let's see...

01:03:24.592 --> 01:03:28.138
"Thank you for attending today's..."

01:03:28.346 --> 01:03:30.890
[chuckles]
I heard your business is soaring.

01:03:30.974 --> 01:03:32.767
Oh, not at all.

01:03:32.851 --> 01:03:36.563
It went a bit viral on social media,

01:03:36.646 --> 01:03:39.899
and let's just say I don't have time
to go to the bathroom.

01:03:39.983 --> 01:03:42.027
-[customer 1] Thank you.
-[Sori] Thank you.

01:03:42.110 --> 01:03:44.195
Hello, what would you like?

01:03:44.279 --> 01:03:46.281
[customer 2] Can we get two packs
of green onion kimchi?

01:03:46.364 --> 01:03:48.033
-And two packs of seaweed stems, please.
-Okay.

01:03:48.116 --> 01:03:49.701
I heard the side dishes here
are really good.

01:03:49.784 --> 01:03:51.745
Really? Thank you.

01:03:51.828 --> 01:03:56.624
Gosh, thanks to Sori,
we went viral on social media.

01:03:56.708 --> 01:03:59.335
I don't even have time
to go to the bathroom.

01:03:59.419 --> 01:04:01.546
You could be buying a building soon.

01:04:01.629 --> 01:04:03.840
-Why not? Let me buy a building.
-[chuckling]

01:04:03.923 --> 01:04:05.258
-Hello.
-Hi.

01:04:05.341 --> 01:04:06.718
[in English] What is this one?

01:04:06.801 --> 01:04:08.803
[in English] It's made
by mixing dried radish

01:04:08.887 --> 01:04:12.766
with seasonings such as
red pepper powder and soy sauce.

01:04:12.849 --> 01:04:13.850
I see.

01:04:13.933 --> 01:04:15.477
-Can I try?
-Yes.

01:04:15.560 --> 01:04:17.062
-Thank you.
-Yes, of course.

01:04:17.145 --> 01:04:18.396
-Here.
-Thank you.

01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:22.650
We have more stuff inside,
so please do take a look.

01:04:22.734 --> 01:04:24.194
Oh, my. [chuckling]

01:04:25.695 --> 01:04:29.491
At this rate, your business might outshine
Myungsoondang overseas.

01:04:29.574 --> 01:04:32.077
Nonsense. [chuckling]

01:04:33.411 --> 01:04:36.831
-It's all thanks to my youngest daughter.
-[chuckles]

01:04:38.416 --> 01:04:43.213
Anyway, how's your son's business?

01:04:43.797 --> 01:04:45.006
What was it?

01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:48.510
I heard it was something to do with games.

01:04:48.593 --> 01:04:49.803
[chuckles sheepishly]

01:04:51.304 --> 01:04:54.766
[sighs softly] Every time I see him,
I think about

01:04:56.184 --> 01:04:57.519
how lucky people without kids are.

01:04:57.602 --> 01:04:58.603
[exclaims]`

01:04:59.687 --> 01:05:02.774
-[softly] It's because he's a son.
-[chuckles softly]

01:05:02.857 --> 01:05:06.027
Is our youngest daughter here
seeing someone?

01:05:06.111 --> 01:05:09.781
[hesitates] Do you have someone
to recommend?

01:05:09.864 --> 01:05:13.034
There's no need to look far
when the right one might be close by.

01:05:13.118 --> 01:05:14.452
Right.

01:05:14.536 --> 01:05:16.121
Let's check out the men from the company.

01:05:16.204 --> 01:05:17.372
-Right.
-Take a look.

01:05:17.455 --> 01:05:18.456
[Miyeon] Well...

01:05:18.915 --> 01:05:20.583
How about someone who runs a game company?

01:05:20.667 --> 01:05:22.627
-[Youngsook] Let's see.
-Me?

01:05:25.130 --> 01:05:28.883
"Now is a reading of the marriage vows
to celebrate the couple's union

01:05:28.967 --> 01:05:30.969
-and a congratulatory speech."
-[exclaims in amazement]

01:05:31.052 --> 01:05:33.096
-Hey, you look like the groom today.
-[chuckles]

01:05:33.179 --> 01:05:34.180
Thank you.

01:05:34.264 --> 01:05:36.182
But don't talk to me. I have to focus.

01:05:36.266 --> 01:05:38.309
Okay, fine.

01:05:38.393 --> 01:05:39.644
Don't make a mistake.

01:05:40.228 --> 01:05:42.438
-Do well.
-Okay, thanks.

01:05:42.522 --> 01:05:43.898
-[chuckles softly]
-[phone vibrating]

01:05:43.982 --> 01:05:45.233
[mumbles]

01:05:48.403 --> 01:05:49.612
Have you arrived?

01:05:49.904 --> 01:05:51.739
[♪ upbeat, whimsical music playing]

01:06:01.541 --> 01:06:02.750
[chuckles softly]

01:06:33.281 --> 01:06:34.365
[Eungsoo clears throat]

01:06:34.449 --> 01:06:36.117
We will now begin

01:06:36.201 --> 01:06:40.580
the wedding of Kim Wooju and Yoo Meri.

01:06:40.663 --> 01:06:44.709
Could all the guests please be seated?

01:06:45.543 --> 01:06:46.544
[clears throat]

01:06:47.128 --> 01:06:50.089
We will now begin the wedding ceremony

01:06:50.173 --> 01:06:53.343
of the groom, Mr. Kim Wooju,
and the bride, Ms. Yoo Meri.

01:06:53.927 --> 01:06:55.511
Bride and groom,

01:06:55.595 --> 01:06:58.014
prepare for your entrance.

01:06:58.097 --> 01:06:59.849
[♪ dreamy pop music playing]

01:07:04.979 --> 01:07:07.565
[Meri] Luck comes in disguise.

01:07:07.649 --> 01:07:08.816
[phone vibrating]

01:07:14.489 --> 01:07:15.490
Hello?

01:07:15.573 --> 01:07:18.326
When the greatest luck
of my life came to me...

01:07:18.409 --> 01:07:20.119
I won?

01:07:20.203 --> 01:07:22.247
But you're the only one I can turn to.

01:07:22.330 --> 01:07:24.415
Could you

01:07:24.499 --> 01:07:25.833
be my husband?

01:07:26.626 --> 01:07:29.087
I thought happiness
was finally coming my way,

01:07:30.421 --> 01:07:33.383
but luck built on lies can't be real.

01:07:35.009 --> 01:07:38.263
Maybe, in all those desperate moments
clinging to that house,

01:07:39.013 --> 01:07:41.307
what I truly wanted

01:07:42.850 --> 01:07:46.145
wasn't a fake home
I had to hide from everyone...

01:07:47.939 --> 01:07:52.527
but a single person who could love me
no matter who I was.

01:07:53.319 --> 01:07:55.238
It's because I like you.

01:07:55.321 --> 01:07:57.949
Whatever it is that you do,

01:07:58.032 --> 01:07:59.993
I'll stay right next to you.

01:08:02.328 --> 01:08:04.122
[Meri] Meeting someone like that.

01:08:06.207 --> 01:08:08.334
Isn't that what luck is really about?

01:08:10.962 --> 01:08:14.799
[Kim Wooju] Such luck comes like fate
in the most desperate moments.

01:08:22.890 --> 01:08:24.142
[crying]

01:08:24.976 --> 01:08:27.603
Who will take care of him?

01:08:27.687 --> 01:08:29.605
-Keep it.
-[teddy recording plays]

01:08:30.064 --> 01:08:31.774
[Kim Wooju] Some days were happy,

01:08:31.858 --> 01:08:33.860
and some days were not.

01:08:35.737 --> 01:08:38.614
Whenever waves of sorrow
and loneliness crashed over me,

01:08:39.866 --> 01:08:41.784
I lost my way and wandered.

01:08:43.619 --> 01:08:45.413
But maybe all that time

01:08:46.289 --> 01:08:49.584
was a path leading me to you.

01:08:55.048 --> 01:08:56.382
As if we had promised to meet

01:08:57.717 --> 01:08:59.344
after a long journey apart.

01:09:00.428 --> 01:09:02.263
[Meri] Every moment of our lives

01:09:03.639 --> 01:09:05.683
was leading us toward one another.

01:09:10.313 --> 01:09:11.314
I love you.

01:09:12.774 --> 01:09:13.775
I love you, too.

01:09:16.402 --> 01:09:18.613
[♪ wedding march playing on piano]

01:09:31.501 --> 01:09:33.544
[guests applauding, whooping]

01:09:40.259 --> 01:09:42.678
[♪ upbeat dreamy music playing]

01:09:55.525 --> 01:09:57.318
[guests continue applauding, whooping]

01:10:18.089 --> 01:10:19.882
[all cheering]

01:10:50.913 --> 01:10:53.583
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:11:37.627 --> 01:11:39.629
Translated by Susanna Kim
